# =============================================================================
# Image2Transcript — .gitignore
#
# Goal: keep the tracked tree limited to the *core, reusable code* (model,
# data-prep, training, eval) and small config/asset files. Everything that is
# large, machine-generated, experiment-specific, internal, or benchmark-only
# is ignored so the public repo stays clean and easy to use.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Raw data & large imaging assets ----------------------------------------
data/
colon/
*.h5ad
*.h5
*.zarr
*.svs
*.tif
*.tiff
*.ome.tif
*.ome.tiff
*.npy
*.npz

# ---- Model weights, embeddings & checkpoints --------------------------------
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.ckpt
ckpt/
pretrained_models/
output*/

# ---- Experiment outputs, logs & figures -------------------------------------
runs/
figs/
logs/
nohup.out
run_local*.log
*.out
*.err
*.log
# Slurm job stdout/stderr dumps (job_<id>_*.out/err)
job_*
*.csv
# keep the curated marker-gene signatures and any split manifests
!gene_signatures/*.csv
!splits/*.csv

# ---- Result artifacts are NOT redistributed ---------------------------------
# Prediction dumps, checkpoints, per-run analysis outputs, rendered figures and
# training logs stay out of the public tree (`runs/`, `figs/`, `*.csv`, `*.log`
# above). The released code regenerates all of them; the artifacts themselves
# are available from the corresponding author on request.

# ---- Internal notes, manuscript & planning docs (not part of the release) ---
CLAUDE.md
docs/
manuscript.md
manuscprits.md
*.draft.md

# ---- External benchmark suites (third-party clones) -------------------------
# GHIST / HEST / SciSt / sCellST are upstream repositories cloned locally to
# produce the Table 5 comparison. They carry their own licences and their own
# git histories, so we do not redistribute them here; scripts/hest_bench/
# documents the exact upstream commits and how to obtain them.
benchmark/

# ---- Analysis, figure & experiment entrypoints ------------------------------
# These are the entrypoints named in the STAI-X reproducibility checklist
# (analysis, figures, TCGA-COAD, HEST-Bench, foundation-model baselines).
# They are part of the public release -- do NOT re-ignore them.
scripts/hest_bench/*.log
scripts/hest_bench/**/__pycache__/

# Unrelated work-in-progress (tPdA single-cell-resolution study, not in the
# submitted paper) and cluster-local environment bootstrap.
scripts/tpda_*.py
scripts/4v100_tpda_*.sh
scripts/1gpu_tpda_*.sh
scripts/setup_scellst_env.sh
scripts/4v100_scellst.sh

# ---- Dev / analysis notebooks (keep only predict.ipynb as the usage demo) ---
image2transcripts.ipynb
validation.ipynb

# ---- Scratch / editor / OS cruft --------------------------------------------
Untitled
**/Untitled
.codex
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
